From: MythosOfs <98063411+MythosOfs@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Ocarina of Time: workaround on by default

Port of Orchid 5b5c31642 by MythosOfs. Default is now on for this title;
EDEN_NX2_OOT_VISUAL_WORKAROUND=0 turns it off. Each edited shader logs
"TEMPORARY OoT visual workaround: shader <hash>, <n> scalar edits"; 0 edits
means the shader's shape differs and it was left alone.
---
 docs/OOT_VISUAL_WORKAROUND.md                        | 5 +++--
 src/shader_recompiler/ir_opt/oot_visual_workaround.h | 2 +-
 src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp | 3 ++-
 3 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/OOT_VISUAL_WORKAROUND.md b/docs/OOT_VISUAL_WORKAROUND.md
index 464847efe9..fda64e6a46 100644
--- a/docs/OOT_VISUAL_WORKAROUND.md
+++ b/docs/OOT_VISUAL_WORKAROUND.md
@@ -1,10 +1,11 @@
 # Ocarina of Time visual workaround (temporary)
 
-This is a temporary, opt-in visual workaround for The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time
+This is a temporary visual workaround for The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time
 (`0400486024DEC000`). It is not an emulator fix. It edits two shaders of this game so the
 outdoor haze and exposure look closer to the reference. The root cause of the haze is still open.
 
-Set `EDEN_NX2_OOT_VISUAL_WORKAROUND=1` to enable it. Any other value, or no value, leaves it off.
+It is on by default for this title. Set `EDEN_NX2_OOT_VISUAL_WORKAROUND=0` to turn it
+off, for example for an A/B comparison.
 Each edited shader logs `TEMPORARY OoT visual workaround: shader <hash>, <n> scalar edits` at
 warning level. An edit count of 0 means the shader no longer has the expected shape and was left
 unchanged.
diff --git a/src/shader_recompiler/ir_opt/oot_visual_workaround.h b/src/shader_recompiler/ir_opt/oot_visual_workaround.h
index cbcbab5aad..1bce69f415 100644
--- a/src/shader_recompiler/ir_opt/oot_visual_workaround.h
+++ b/src/shader_recompiler/ir_opt/oot_visual_workaround.h
@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@
 
 namespace Shader::Optimization {
 
-// TEMPORARY opt-in visual workaround for Ocarina of Time, not an emulator fix.
+// TEMPORARY visual workaround for Ocarina of Time, not an emulator fix.
 inline std::optional<size_t> ApplyOotVisualWorkaround(IR::Program& program, u64 title_id,
                                                      u64 shader_hash, bool enabled) {
     if (!enabled || title_id != 0x0400486024DEC000ULL) {
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
index 5b008b20af..f32a73e37c 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
@@ -397,7 +397,8 @@ PipelineCache::PipelineCache(Tegra::MaxwellDeviceMemoryManager& device_memory_,
                                 !DriverCachesPipelines(device_)},
       oot_visual_workaround{[] {
           const char* value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_OOT_VISUAL_WORKAROUND");
-          return value != nullptr && std::string_view{value} == "1";
+          // On by default for Ocarina of Time; EDEN_NX2_OOT_VISUAL_WORKAROUND=0 turns it off.
+          return value == nullptr || std::string_view{value} != "0";
       }()},
       workers(device.HasBrokenParallelShaderCompiling() ? 1ULL : GetTotalPipelineWorkers(),
               "VkPipelineBuilder", {}, Common::ThreadPlacement::Background),
